0059 — fit, wrap and clamp a text run in layout, and record what was left out.

A template filled from data needs a field's size and lines decided against
the box the field lands in. Until now only a generator could decide them,
before the build, against a box it computed itself: it cannot see a box
flex sizes, and a decision it got wrong reached the frame as a box pushed
out of its container. This patch makes three declarations on a `<Text>`
that the core evaluates at layout, against the content box the solver
offers the text leaf, and records what it chose:

- `text-fit-[min..max]` / `text-fit-[a,b,...]`: a ladder of font slots,
  largest first. The run is laid out at the first rung whose block holds
  the box, and at the last when none does.
- `text-wrap`: the run wraps to the content width at the break
  opportunities it carries — a run of spaces, dropped at the break, and
  U+200B, which is never looked up or drawn. '\n' always breaks. No
  language rule enters the core: a generator writes U+200B where its own
  segmenter allows a break.
- `line-clamp-N`: the first N lines are kept and the last ends in U+2026,
  or "..." when the face maps no U+2026, losing characters from its end
  (a combining mark with the character it sits on) until the ellipsis fits.

A rung holds when its widest line fits the width, its lines times its line
height fit the height when the node bounds its height (`h-*`, `h-full`,
`max-h-*`), it has no more lines than the clamp keeps, and no segment had
to be cut between its own characters. A segment wider than the line is cut
only at the rung taken when no rung holds, and the cut is counted.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts` and the generated `spec.rs`, microts `spec.rs`
  and `component-types-microts.ts`: props `textFit0` (101) and `textFit1`
  (102), one byte per rung, slot + 1, rungs 0..3 and 4..7; `lineClamp`
  (103); `textWrap` (104). All four dirty layout. `TEXT_FIT_MAX_RUNGS = 8`.
  No draw op, no table, no anim bit.
- `engine/core/src/text_fit.rs` (new): `FitSpec` from a resolved style,
  `Fonts::fit_run`, and `Fitted`, the record. Widths are summed per line
  exactly as `Fonts::measure_run` sums them, so a fitted block measures as
  its laid-out text and the box layout reserves is the box paint fills.
- `engine/core/src/layout.rs`: a text leaf's `MeasureCtx` carries its fit
  declaration and whether the node bounds its height; the measure closure
  takes `fonts` and the offered `AvailableSpace` (a definite width is the
  line length, min-content is every segment on its own line and none cut,
  max-content is unbounded) and answers with the fitted block, cached per
  box. Readback fits the content box the solver settled on and stores the
  record on the node (`Node::text_fit`). A node declaring none of the
  three resolves to no fit and lays out as it did.
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: `emit_text` draws the record's slot and text.
- `engine/core/src/lib.rs`: a text swap in a fixed cell relayouts a fitted
  run; `debug_text_fit(id)` and `debug_text_fit_word(i)` read the record.
  `engine/wasm/src/lib.rs` exports them as `ui_debug_text_fit` and
  `ui_debug_text_fit_word`.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: the three utilities. A range is the
  ten-percent ladder from its top (each rung the one above times 9/10
  rounded up, in integers; `[48..88]` is 88, 80, 72, 65, 59, 54, 49, 48);
  more than eight rungs is refused naming them, a text size beside a ladder
  is refused, and every rung's slot is in `usedFontSlots`. `drawnCodepoints`
  carries U+2026 when any record clamps, and `tools/build.ts` bakes it.

Why it is class upstream: every piece is the declaration layer — a class
literal, a style table, layout and the slot a GLYPH_RUN names — and none of
it depends on a target. A native-text host keeps its own measurer for every
run but these: a fitted run is measured and drawn from the atlas, as a
tracked run already is.

Tests, in `engine/core/src/text_fit_tests.rs`, each red under the edit named
(`baselines/text-fit/redcheck.py` in the motion repository makes the edit,
runs the test and restores it):

- `the_largest_rung_that_holds_is_taken`.
- `a_block_too_tall_for_its_box_gives_way_to_the_next_rung`: red with the
  height test removed from `holds`.
- `a_rung_that_must_cut_a_segment_does_not_hold`: red with `w.split == 0`
  removed from `holds`.
- `a_line_breaks_at_spaces_and_u200b_and_u200b_is_never_drawn`: red with
  U+200B read as part of a segment.
- `a_clamp_keeps_its_lines_ends_with_an_ellipsis_and_counts_what_it_left_out`:
  red with the dropped count left at zero, with the ellipsis loop accepting
  the line as it is, and with a mark cut from its base.
- `a_face_with_no_ellipsis_ends_a_clamp_with_three_periods`.
- `a_fitted_block_measures_as_its_laid_out_text`: red with tracking left out
  of the pen and with the clamped line's old width kept.
- `the_ladder_unpacks_from_its_two_words`: red with the ladder read from the
  first word only.
- `layout_records_the_fit_and_paint_draws_it`: red with paint drawing the
  style's slot, with a node's height never a bound, and with readback
  fitting an unbounded height.

